From 0caa90b06f79bbd5160a368e4fd5b6041869bb28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: update the text of an existing placeholder

init_placeholder_container_if_necessary returned
`placeholder_container.root_element()` for an existing container, which
resolves to Element::root_element (the topmost element of the UA shadow tree)
rather than rooting the Dom. Its first child is not a text node, so changing
an existing placeholder never reached the placeholder text and the old text
stayed on screen. Root the stored container instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 components/script/dom/html/input_element/text_input_widget.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/script/dom/html/input_element/text_input_widget.rs b/components/script/dom/html/input_element/text_input_widget.rs
index 2cd0a686f1c..a0939d3d9ae 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/html/input_element/text_input_widget.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/html/input_element/text_input_widget.rs
@@ -148,7 +148,7 @@ impl TextInputWidgetShadowTree {
         element: &impl TextControlElement,
     ) -> Option<DomRoot<Element>> {
         if let Some(placeholder_container) = &*self.placeholder_container.borrow() {
-            return Some(placeholder_container.root_element());
+            return Some(placeholder_container.as_rooted());
         }
         // If there is no placeholder text and we haven't already created one then it is
         // not necessary to initialize a new placeholder container.
